  "decision_list": [
    "no published chunk and no gap -> no-squashfs-chunk",
    "gap missing-extractor-dependency -> dep-missing-be if the dependency is sasquatch-v4be, else dep-missing-le (handler is squashfs_v4_be / squashfs_v4_le respectively)",
    "gap extractor-failure + stderr contains 'suggests a SquashFS image of a different endianess' + the recorded argv has no -be -> avm-marker-be-dropped",
    "gap extractor-failure + stderr contains 'Block size too small' -> version-minor-mismatch",
    "gap extractor-failure + stderr contains 'read_id_table: failed to read id table block' + argv has -be -> body-extractor-failure",
    "gap unpublished-entry -> in-tree-symlink-metadata",
    "diagnostic MaliciousSymlinkRemoved and no gap -> escaping-symlink-removed",
    "otherwise -> clean (handler squashfs_v4_be and squashfs_v4_le both map to the label clean)"
  ],
  "decision_list_matches": 20,
  "decision_list_total": 20,
  "order_matters": [
    "avm-marker-be-dropped and body-extractor-failure share handler, extraction_failed, coverage, gap kind (extractor-failure), diagnostic typename (ExtractCommandFailedReport) and exit code 1; only the diagnostic argv (-be present or absent) and the first stderr line separate them, so a gap-kind-only or diagnostic-typename-only table cannot label them.",
    "both also emit 'read_id_table: failed to read id table block', so a table that matches that string first mislabels the AVM carrier as body damage."
  ]
